  <sport:Coach rdf:about="#PepGuardiola">
    <sport:firstName>Pep</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Guardiola</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1971-01-18</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Spain</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">17</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:titlesWon rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">37</sport:titlesWon>
    <sport:coachingStyle>Possession-based</sport:coachingStyle>
    <sport:description>Revolutionized modern football with his possession-based 'tiki-taka' philosophy. Pep Guardiola has won league titles in Spain, Germany, and England, making him one of the most successful managers in history. His tactical innovations, attention to detail, and ability to develop young talents have influenced coaches worldwide. Under his guidance, teams don't just win—they dominate with style.</sport:description>
    <sport:philosophy>Possession-based football, High pressing, Positional play, Total football principles</sport:philosophy>
    <sport:coachesAthlete rdf:resource="#LionelMessi" />
    <sport:coachesAthlete rdf:resource="#ErlingHaaland" />
  </sport:Coach>

  <sport:Coach rdf:about="#CarloAncelotti">
    <sport:firstName>Carlo</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Ancelotti</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1959-06-10</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Italy</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:titlesWon rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">26</sport:titlesWon>
    <sport:coachingStyle>Defensive</sport:coachingStyle>
    <sport:description>One of only three managers to win the UEFA Champions League four times. Carlo Ancelotti is known for his calm demeanor, tactical flexibility, and exceptional ability to manage superstars. His man-management skills and tactical adaptability have brought success across multiple top European clubs including AC Milan, Chelsea, PSG, Bayern Munich, and Real Madrid.</sport:description>
    <sport:philosophy>Tactical flexibility, Player management, Defensive organization, Counter-attacking, Calm leadership</sport:philosophy>
    <sport:coachesAthlete rdf:resource="#CristianoRonaldo" />
    <sport:coachesAthlete rdf:resource="#KylianMbappe" />
  </sport:Coach>

  <sport:Coach rdf:about="#JurgenKlopp">
    <sport:firstName>Jurgen</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Klopp</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1967-06-16</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Germany</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">23</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:titlesWon rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</sport:titlesWon>
    <sport:coachingStyle>Gegenpressing</sport:coachingStyle>
    <sport:description>The charismatic German manager known for his 'gegenpressing' or 'heavy metal football' style. Klopp transformed Liverpool into European champions and ended their 30-year wait for a Premier League title. His passion, emotional leadership, and connection with fans are unmatched. He builds teams that press relentlessly and play with incredible intensity and unity.</sport:description>
    <sport:philosophy>Gegenpressing, High-intensity football, Emotional leadership, Team unity, Full-throttle mentality</sport:philosophy>
  </sport:Coach>

  <sport:Coach rdf:about="#ZinedineZidane">
    <sport:firstName>Zinedine</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Zidane</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1972-06-23</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>France</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:titlesWon rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">11</sport:titlesWon>
    <sport:coachingStyle>Counter-attacking</sport:coachingStyle>
    <sport:description>A legendary player turned legendary coach, Zidane won three consecutive Champions League titles with Real Madrid—a feat unmatched in the modern era. His calm presence, tactical acumen, and ability to manage one of football's most star-studded squads demonstrated his natural leadership. As both player and coach, Zidane represents football excellence at its highest level.</sport:description>
    <sport:philosophy>Counter-attacking football, Player empowerment, Rotation management, Tactical adaptability, Star management</sport:philosophy>
  </sport:Coach>

  <sport:Coach rdf:about="#DiegoSimeone">
    <sport:firstName>Diego</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Simeone</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1970-04-28</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Argentina</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">20</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:titlesWon rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">8</sport:titlesWon>
    <sport:coachingStyle>Defensive</sport:coachingStyle>
    <sport:description>The Argentine firebrand known for his intense, defensive tactical approach. Simeone transformed Atletico Madrid into a powerhouse, breaking the Barcelona-Real Madrid duopoly in La Liga. His teams are known for their incredible work ethic, defensive solidity, and never-say-die attitude. His passionate touchline presence and warrior mentality inspire total commitment from his players.</sport:description>
    <sport:philosophy>Defensive solidity, Counter-attacking, High work rate, Mental resilience, Warrior mentality</sport:philosophy>
  </sport:Coach>

  
  <sport:Referee rdf:about="#PierluigiCollina">
    <sport:firstName>Pierluigi</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Collina</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1960-02-13</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Italy</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:matchesOfficiated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">430</sport:matchesOfficiated>
    <sport:description>Widely regarded as the greatest referee of all time, Pierluigi Collina officiated the 2002 World Cup Final and multiple Champions League finals. His distinctive bald appearance and authoritative presence commanded respect from players and coaches alike. Known for his exceptional decision-making, consistency, and ability to control high-pressure matches, he set the standard for modern refereeing.</sport:description>
    <sport:expertise>Match control, Consistency, Communication, Decision-making under pressure, Authority</sport:expertise>
  </sport:Referee>

  <sport:Referee rdf:about="#HowardWebb">
    <sport:firstName>Howard</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Webb</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1971-07-14</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>England</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">18</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:matchesOfficiated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">315</sport:matchesOfficiated>
    <sport:description>The English referee who officiated both the 2010 World Cup Final and Champions League Final in the same year—a unique achievement in refereeing history. Webb was known for his calm demeanor, excellent communication with players, and ability to manage high-stakes matches. He retired as one of the most respected officials in world football and now serves as Chief Refereeing Officer for the Premier League.</sport:description>
    <sport:expertise>High-pressure situations, Player management, Consistent decision-making, Communication, Big-match temperament</sport:expertise>
  </sport:Referee>

  <sport:Referee rdf:about="#BjornKuipers">
    <sport:firstName>Bjorn</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Kuipers</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1973-03-28</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Netherlands</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">21</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:matchesOfficiated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">387</sport:matchesOfficiated>
  </sport:Referee>

  <sport:Referee rdf:about="#FelixBrych">
    <sport:firstName>Felix</sport:firstName>
    <sport:lastName>Brych</sport:lastName>
    <sport:birthDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">1975-08-03</sport:birthDate>
    <sport:nationality>Germany</sport:nationality>
    <sport:experienceYears rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">24</sport:experienceYears>
    <sport:matchesOfficiated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">402</sport:matchesOfficiated>
    <sport:description>Germany's most prominent referee and a lawyer by profession. Felix Brych has officiated multiple Champions League finals and major international tournaments. His calm authority, legal precision in decision-making, and deep understanding of the game have made him one of UEFA's most trusted officials. He consistently handles the biggest matches in European football with confidence and fairness.</sport:description>
    <sport:expertise>Game management, Legal precision in decisions, Experience in top-level matches, Calm authority, Fair play enforcement</sport:expertise>
  </sport:Referee>

</rdf:RDF>